hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2153","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Give the prescribed shares to those who are entitled to them, and whatever remains after that, it belongs to the nearest male relative (i.e., the 'Asabah)."
"2154","Someone asked Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) about the inheritance of a daughter, a granddaughter, and a sister. He replied: ""Half is for the daughter and half is for the sister. And you should go and ask Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them both); I am sure he will give the same answer as I did."" So they asked him, and Abu Musa's answer was mentioned to him. He said: ""If I give this answer, I would go astray and never be guided. I will give the same ruling as the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave in this matter: half for the daughter, one-sixth for the granddaughter—this makes two-thirds—and the remaining one-third is for the sister."" (The questioner says:) ""Then we returned to Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) and informed him of Ibn Mas'ud's (may Allah be pleased with them both) verdict. He said: 'As long as this scholar (i.e., Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with them both) is among you, never ask me again.'"
"2155","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The freed slave of every nation will be counted among that nation."
"2156","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The nephew of every nation will be counted among that nation."
"2157","Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever claims someone other than his (real) father as his father, knowing that he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden for him."" (The narrator of the hadith, Uthman, said:) I narrated this hadith to Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: My ears also heard this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I remembered it."
"2158","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""(O people!) Do not disown your fathers, for disowning one's father is disbelief."
